{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 0, "cost_per_unit": "Each leaf costs several Python calls per pass (a match closure, then Token.match or imt, then __contains__ tuple slicing), about 0.3-1 us each. A regex sweep over the ordered SQL_REGEX list runs per lexed token. Each new group re-flattens its whole subtree to compute its value.", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Doubling the number of statements roughly doubles the time, since each statement is processed independently. Doubling a single statement's length grows its time a bit more than 2x: the flatten-based group value is O(n*depth), and the repeated forward scans of _token_matching add super-linear terms.", "gap": "format and parse lex the same statement string twice. About 6 of the 11 _group passes (typecasts, tzcasts, typed literal x2, assignment, arrays, often period) walk the whole tree and never fire on plain SELECT/INSERT. TokenList construction re-walks nested generators, costing O(leaves x depth) per g", "least_work": "Lex each distinct statement text once. Run only the grouping passes whose trigger tokens actually occur in the statement. Compute a group's text from its direct children.", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 1, "unit_count": "About 66k lexer yields, 72k _group calls, 9.8k _group_matching calls, 751k Token.match, 524k imt, 499k _TokenType.__contains__ and 743k flatten calls. That is roughly 22k leaf tokens, each lexed 3 times (split, format, parse) and grouped twice.", "unit_of_work": "A lexed leaf token, processed by the lexer and splitter and then visited by each grouping pass (about 25 recursive passes) on every format and parse call."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 2, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "elimin