{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 12, "cost_per_unit": "Total is about 3.0 s (get_tokens self time 0.306 s is 10.2 %), so about 45 us per lexed token end to end. Per character position the lexer runs a Python-level loop over the whole regex table. Each grouping pass makes closure calls per token, and flatten resumes a chain of nested generators for every", "deal_round": 2, "doubling": "Roughly linear in the number of statements and tokens, so time doubles. Per statement the grouping cost is passes x tokens x tree depth, and the reindent offset recomputation via flatten is superlinear in statement length.", "gap": "Large constant factors: Python-level iteration over the regex list at every position, a closure call per token inside token_next scans, and nested yield-from chains that make each leaf cost one resumption per tree level. These come on top of the redundant re-lexing and re-grouping already on the tab", "least_work": "Lex each character once using C-level regex matching, make a constant number of passes over the leaf tokens to group them, and flatten in one step per leaf.", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 1, "unit_count": "About 66k get_tokens resumptions, i.e. roughly 22k tokens per pass and about 137 tokens per statement. Each token is then visited by about 25 grouping passes: 751k match calls, 524k imt calls, 743k flatten resumptions and 105k _token_matching scans.", "unit_of_work": "One lexed token carried through splitting, grouping, filtering and serialisation. Each statement is lexed three times: once by split over the whole script, once by format and once by parse."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 1, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "f995be7d"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claud