{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 3, "cost_per_unit": "Under the profiler, roughly 1.0 s / 51,200 is about 19 us per top-level key/value line. Each line makes about 10 Python calls (key_value_rule, parse_key_value_pair, parse_key, parse_key_part, 3-4 skip_chars, parse_value, regex). skip_chars averages about 0.18 us and usually advances 0 or 1 character", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Linear: twice the tables gives twice the statements and values, so roughly twice the wall time. Nothing in the hot path is superlinear for this workload.", "gap": "Most of the time is interpreter call and setup overhead, not character work. Whitespace skips that advance 0 or 1 character still pay for a full call with try/except, and keys go through 3 nested functions plus separate skips around '='. Fusing these per-token steps into single checks or matches is ", "least_work": "One left-to-right pass over the characters, with one dispatch or regex match per token (key, '=', value, separator) and one dict insertion per value.", "library": "tomli", "run": 1, "unit_count": "Over 8 parses: 51,200 key_value_rule calls, 60,800 parse_key_value_pair calls, 108,800 parse_value calls, 67,200 parse_key calls, 70,400 parse_key_part calls, 502,400 skip_chars calls and 115,200 skip_comments_and_array_ws calls.", "unit_of_work": "One TOML statement (mostly key = value lines) and the values inside it, each parsed by a chain of small Python functions that look at one character at a time."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 1, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "62029649"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "62029649"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "view_sha": "62029649"}, {"lane": "far", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "62029649"}, {"lane": "recombine", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "62029649"}, {"lane": "reso